IMPORT prelude

-- Societies Act 1966 (Singapore) -- what a "society" is, who must register and how,
-- and the duties of a registered society: ss 2 to 13 and the Schedule.
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation in force from 1 November 2024, as
-- deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/SA1966.txt. (The deposited arrangement of
-- sections numbers "Interpretation" as s 3; the body of the Act numbers it s 2, and
-- this encoding follows the body.)
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. A citation count across the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository
-- found 38 Acts that cite the Societies Act 1966, for an Act of 94,000 characters. It is
-- also the Act that decides whether an ordinary group of ten people is breaking the law.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No
-- pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: ss 3 (appointment of the Registrar), 5 (the annual list), 33A and 34
-- (powers to amend the Schedule and make regulations), 38 (transitional); and no regulation,
-- notification or exemption order under the Act was retrieved. In particular the
-- exemptions that ordinary social groups rely on in practice are not here.

§ `Societies Act 1966 -- ss 2 to 13 and the Schedule`

§§ `2 -- what a "society" is`

-- s 2: "'society' includes any club, company, partnership or association of 10 OR MORE
-- PERSONS, WHATEVER ITS NATURE OR OBJECT, but does not include --
--   (a) any company registered under any written law relating to companies in force in
--       Singapore;
--   (b) any company or association constituted under any written law;
--   (c) any limited liability partnership registered under the Limited Liability Partnerships
--       Act 2005;
--   (d) any trade union registered or required to be registered;
--   (da) any platform work association registered or required to be registered under the
--        Platform Workers Act 2024;
--   (e) any cooperative society registered as such under any written law;
--   (f) any mutual benefit organisation registered as such under any written law;
--   (g) any company, association or partnership, CONSISTING OF NOT MORE THAN 20 PERSONS,
--       formed for the SOLE PURPOSE of carrying on any lawful business that has for its
--       object the acquisition of gain by the company, association or partnership, or the
--       individual members thereof;
--   (h) any class, society or association of foreign insurers carrying on insurance business
--       in Singapore under a foreign insurer scheme under Part 2A of the Insurance Act 1966;
--       or
--   (i) any school or management committee of a school constituted under any law regulating
--       schools."
--
-- THE REACH IS WIDE AND THE EXCLUSIONS ARE NARROW. Ten people who meet regularly for any
-- purpose at all form a society unless an exclusion applies, and the only exclusion for an
-- ordinary non-profit group is registration under some other law. The business exclusion in
-- (g) is confined to a group of no more than 20 formed for the sole purpose of gain: a
-- profit-making partnership or association of 21 or more that is not a registered company,
-- and a ten-person group formed for gain AND anything else, are both societies.
DECLARE GroupFacts HAS
    `is a club, company, partnership or association` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the number of persons` IS A NUMBER
    `is a company registered under company law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a company or association constituted under a written law` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a limited liability partnership registered under the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a trade union registered or required to be registered` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a platform work association registered or required to be registered` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a cooperative society registered as such` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a mutual benefit organisation registered as such` IS A BOOLEAN
    `was formed for the sole purpose of carrying on a lawful business with the object of gain` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a class, society or association of foreign insurers under a foreign insurer scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a school or the management committee of a school` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the group` IS A GroupFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the group falls within the business exclusion in paragraph (g)` IF
        `the group`'s `was formed for the sole purpose of carrying on a lawful business with the object of gain`
    AND `the group`'s `the number of persons` AT MOST 20

GIVEN `the group` IS A GroupFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the group falls within an exclusion in section 2` IF
        `the group`'s `is a company registered under company law`
    OR  `the group`'s `is a company or association constituted under a written law`
    OR  `the group`'s `is a limited liability partnership registered under the Limited Liability Partnerships Act 2005`
    OR  `the group`'s `is a trade union registered or required to be registered`
    OR  `the group`'s `is a platform work association registered or required to be registered`
    OR  `the group`'s `is a cooperative society registered as such`
    OR  `the group`'s `is a mutual benefit organisation registered as such`
    OR  `the group falls within the business exclusion in paragraph (g)` `the group`
    OR  `the group`'s `is a class, society or association of foreign insurers under a foreign insurer scheme`
    OR  `the group`'s `is a school or the management committee of a school`

GIVEN `the group` IS A GroupFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the group is a society` IF
        `the group`'s `is a club, company, partnership or association`
    AND `the group`'s `the number of persons` AT LEAST 10
    AND NOT `the group falls within an exclusion in section 2` `the group`

-- s 2: "'officer' means the president, the secretary and members of the committee of a society
-- and includes persons holding positions analogous to those of president, secretary or member
-- of a committee". The treasurer is therefore an officer only as a committee member or by
-- analogy.
DECLARE Position IS ONE OF
    `the president`
    `the secretary`
    `a member of the committee`
    `a person holding a position analogous to one of those`
    `the treasurer who is not on the committee`
    `an ordinary member`

GIVEN `the position` IS A Position
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is an officer of the society` IF
    CONSIDER `the position`
    WHEN `the president` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the secretary` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a member of the committee` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a person holding a position analogous to one of those` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `The Schedule -- the "specified societies"`

-- The Schedule lists thirteen kinds of society. A society that falls within any of them is a
-- "specified society" for s 4: it must register under s 4 rather than s 4A, and s 4 gives the
-- Registrar more grounds, and some mandatory ones, for refusing.
--   1. object, purpose or activity (primary or otherwise) is to represent, promote any cause or
--      interest of, or discuss any issue relating to, any RELIGION, ETHNIC GROUP, CLAN,
--      NATIONALITY or a class defined by reference to GENDER OR SEXUAL ORIENTATION;
--   2. any POLITICAL ASSOCIATION (defined in s 2: a political party and any society the Minister
--      declares by order to be one);
--   3. uses the word "NATIONAL" or "SINGAPORE" in its name, except where "Singapore" or an
--      abbreviation is used to indicate the place of registration;
--   4. represents persons who advocate, promotes, or discusses any issue relating to any CIVIL OR
--      POLITICAL RIGHT (including human rights, environmental rights and animal rights);
--   5. discusses any matter relating to the GOVERNANCE OF THE SINGAPORE SOCIETY;
--   6. promotes or discusses the use or status of any LANGUAGE;
--   7. formed under the instruction of a FOREIGN GOVERNMENT or an organisation affiliated to one;
--   8. formed under the instruction of a FOREIGN ORGANISATION, or affiliated to one, or whose
--      MAJOR SOURCE OF FUNDING IS FROM OUTSIDE SINGAPORE, but not the Rotaract Club, the Rotary
--      Club, the Toastmasters Club or the Lions Club;
--   9. any ALUMNI of an educational institution not established in Singapore;
--   10. any society which has an OFFICE BEARER who (a) was holding office in a society dissolved
--       under s 24 less than 3 years ago; (b) while a member of any society was convicted of an
--       offence involving the unlawful expenditure of its funds; or (c) has been previously
--       declared in writing BY THE MINISTER to be unfit to act as an officer of a society;
--   11. promotes, discusses or trains in any form of PUGILISTIC OR MARTIAL ARTS;
--   12. related to controlled drugs or psychoactive substances, games of chance, betting,
--       lotteries and prizes by chance, or the provision of sexual services for payment;
--   13. object is to commit, or promote or facilitate the commission of, an OFFENCE.
--
-- Three things in the wording matter.
--   * "primary or otherwise": an incidental activity is enough for items 1, 4, 5, 6, 11 and 12.
--     A hiking club that sometimes discusses a language policy is specified.
--   * Item 3's exception for "Singapore" as a place of registration does not extend to
--     "National".
--   * Item 10(c) speaks of a declaration "by the Minister". The Act gives the Registrar, not the
--     Minister, the power to declare a person unfit (s 12(1)(b)). No section confers the
--     declaration the Schedule refers to.
DECLARE SpecifiedFacts HAS
    `purpose touches religion, an ethnic group, a clan, a nationality, or a class by gender or sexual orientation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a political association` IS A BOOLEAN
    `name uses the word National` IS A BOOLEAN
    `name uses the word Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the word Singapore only indicates the place of registration` IS A BOOLEAN
    `purpose touches a civil or political right` IS A BOOLEAN
    `purpose touches the governance of the Singapore society` IS A BOOLEAN
    `purpose touches the use or status of a language` IS A BOOLEAN
    `formed under the instruction of a foreign government or an affiliated organisation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `formed under the instruction of, or affiliated to, a foreign organisation, or mainly funded from outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is the Rotaract Club, the Rotary Club, the Toastmasters Club or the Lions Club` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is the alumni of an educational institution not established in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has an office bearer who was an officer of a society dissolved under section 24 less than 3 years ago` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has an office bearer convicted, as a member of a society, of an offence involving unlawful expenditure of its funds` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has an office bearer previously declared unfit in writing by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
    `purpose touches pugilistic or martial arts` IS A BOOLEAN
    `purpose touches controlled drugs, games of chance, betting, lotteries or sexual services for reward` IS A BOOLEAN
    `purpose is to commit or promote an offence` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the society` IS A SpecifiedFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the society is a specified society` IF
        `the society`'s `purpose touches religion, an ethnic group, a clan, a nationality, or a class by gender or sexual orientation`
    OR  `the society`'s `is a political association`
    OR  `the society`'s `name uses the word National`
    OR  (    `the society`'s `name uses the word Singapore`
         AND NOT `the society`'s `the word Singapore only indicates the place of registration`)
    OR  `the society`'s `purpose touches a civil or political right`
    OR  `the society`'s `purpose touches the governance of the Singapore society`
    OR  `the society`'s `purpose touches the use or status of a language`
    OR  `the society`'s `formed under the instruction of a foreign government or an affiliated organisation`
    OR  (    `the society`'s `formed under the instruction of, or affiliated to, a foreign organisation, or mainly funded from outside Singapore`
         AND NOT `the society`'s `it is the Rotaract Club, the Rotary Club, the Toastmasters Club or the Lions Club`)
    OR  `the society`'s `is the alumni of an educational institution not established in Singapore`
    OR  `the society`'s `has an office bearer who was an officer of a society dissolved under section 24 less than 3 years ago`
    OR  `the society`'s `has an office bearer convicted, as a member of a society, of an offence involving unlawful expenditure of its funds`
    OR  `the society`'s `has an office bearer previously declared unfit in writing by the Minister`
    OR  `the society`'s `purpose touches pugilistic or martial arts`
    OR  `the society`'s `purpose touches controlled drugs, games of chance, betting, lotteries or sexual services for reward`
    OR  `the society`'s `purpose is to commit or promote an offence`

-- The gap in item 10(c): the Registrar's declaration under s 12(1)(b) is not "by the Minister".
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `any section of the Act empowers the Minister to declare a person unfit to act as an officer` IF
    FALSE

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 12(1)(b) empowers the Registrar to declare a person unfit to act as an officer` IF
    TRUE

§§ `4 -- registration of a specified society`

-- s 4(1): the Registrar "may" register a specified society.
-- s 4(2): the Registrar "SHALL REFUSE" to register a specified society if satisfied that --
--   (a) its rules are insufficient to provide for its proper management and control;
--   (b) it is likely to be used for unlawful purposes or for purposes prejudicial to public
--       peace, welfare or good order in Singapore;
--   (c) the application does not comply with the Act or the regulations;
--   (d) it would be contrary to Singapore's national security or interest for it to be
--       registered; or
--   (e) if it is a political association, its rules do not confine membership to citizens of
--       Singapore or it has such affiliation or connection with an organisation outside
--       Singapore as the Registrar considers contrary to national security or interest.
-- s 4(3): the Registrar "MAY" refuse if (a) the society is a branch of, or affiliated or
-- connected with, a society dissolved under s 24 or previously refused registration; (b) a dispute
-- exists among the members as to who are to be officers or hold or administer property; or (c)
-- the name is (i) likely to mislead as to character or purpose or so nearly resembles another's as
-- to deceive, (ii) identical to another existing society's, or (iii) in the Registrar's opinion
-- UNDESIRABLE.
-- s 4(3A): the Registrar may also refuse unless the rules include or exclude whatever provisions
-- the Registrar directs.
-- s 4(4): an aggrieved person may within 30 days appeal to the Minister, whose decision is final.
DECLARE Section4Facts HAS
    `the Registrar is satisfied the rules are insufficient for proper management and control` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Registrar is satisfied it is likely to be used for unlawful purposes or purposes prejudicial to public peace, welfare or good order` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the application does not comply with the Act or the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Registrar is satisfied registration would be contrary to national security or interest` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a political association whose rules do not confine membership to citizens` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a political association with a foreign connection the Registrar considers contrary to national security or interest` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a branch of, or connected with, a dissolved or previously refused society` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a dispute exists among members as to officers or property` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the name is misleading, deceptively similar, identical to another's, or undesirable in the Registrar's opinion` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the rules lack provisions the Registrar has directed` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the application` IS A Section4Facts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar must refuse a specified society` IF
        `the application`'s `the Registrar is satisfied the rules are insufficient for proper management and control`
    OR  `the application`'s `the Registrar is satisfied it is likely to be used for unlawful purposes or purposes prejudicial to public peace, welfare or good order`
    OR  `the application`'s `the application does not comply with the Act or the regulations`
    OR  `the application`'s `the Registrar is satisfied registration would be contrary to national security or interest`
    OR  `the application`'s `it is a political association whose rules do not confine membership to citizens`
    OR  `the application`'s `it is a political association with a foreign connection the Registrar considers contrary to national security or interest`

GIVEN `the application` IS A Section4Facts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar may refuse a specified society` IF
        `the Registrar must refuse a specified society` `the application`
    OR  `the application`'s `it is a branch of, or connected with, a dissolved or previously refused society`
    OR  `the application`'s `a dispute exists among members as to officers or property`
    OR  `the application`'s `the name is misleading, deceptively similar, identical to another's, or undesirable in the Registrar's opinion`
    OR  `the application`'s `the rules lack provisions the Registrar has directed`

§§ `4A -- registration of a society that is not specified`

-- s 4A(3): the Registrar "may" register; (3A) "MUST REFUSE" if satisfied that (a) it is likely to
-- be used for unlawful purposes or purposes prejudicial to public peace, welfare or good order, or
-- (b) registration would be contrary to national security or interest.
--
-- Only two grounds are mandatory, and there is no mandatory ground about the sufficiency of the
-- rules or the name. But "may" with no stated grounds leaves the Registrar free to refuse for any
-- reason, so the narrower list of mandatory grounds does not narrow the discretion: it only marks
-- what the Registrar has no choice about.
-- s 4A(5): where the Registrar considers a society registered under s 4A ought to have been
-- registered under s 4 because it is specified, and it qualifies, the Registrar "may determine that
-- the society be treated as being registered under section 4", may recover the fee difference as a
-- debt, and the society is deemed registered under s 4 from the date of its registration. s 4A(8):
-- the Minister's s 24 power is preserved.
-- s 4A(7): an appeal against a refusal lies to the Minister within 30 days; the decision is final.
DECLARE Section4AFacts HAS
    `the Registrar is satisfied it is likely to be used for unlawful purposes or purposes prejudicial to public peace, welfare or good order` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Registrar is satisfied registration would be contrary to national security or interest` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the rules are insufficient for proper management and control` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the name is undesirable in the Registrar's opinion` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the application` IS A Section4AFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar must refuse a society that is not specified` IF
        `the application`'s `the Registrar is satisfied it is likely to be used for unlawful purposes or purposes prejudicial to public peace, welfare or good order`
    OR  `the application`'s `the Registrar is satisfied registration would be contrary to national security or interest`

-- The mandatory refusal grounds in s 4(2)(a) and s 4(3)(c) have no counterpart in s 4A(3A), but
-- nothing stops the Registrar refusing on them.
GIVEN `the application` IS A Section4AFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a mandatory refusal ground in section 4 is absent from section 4A` IF
        `the application`'s `the rules are insufficient for proper management and control`
    OR  `the application`'s `the name is undesirable in the Registrar's opinion`

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 4A confines the Registrar's discretion to refuse to the stated grounds` IF
    FALSE

GIVEN `the Registrar considers it ought to have been registered under section 4` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `it qualifies and could have been registered under section 4` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar may treat a section 4A society as registered under section 4` IF
        `the Registrar considers it ought to have been registered under section 4`
    AND `it qualifies and could have been registered under section 4`

§§ `Appeals to the Minister -- which have a time limit and which do not`

-- s 4(4), 4A(7), 9(4), 11(4): "within 30 days from the date of the decision appeal to the
-- Minister whose decision shall be final". s 13(2): "may appeal against that decision to the
-- Minister whose decision shall be final" -- NO PERIOD STATED.
--
-- No appeal at all is provided against: a notice under s 10 requiring information, an order under
-- s 11A to change a section 4A society's name or rules, a declaration under s 12(1)(b) that a
-- person is unfit to be an officer (the person may only apply to the Minister for permission under
-- s 12(1A)), or an order dissolving a society under s 24.
DECLARE Decision IS ONE OF
    `a refusal to register a specified society under section 4`
    `a refusal to register a society under section 4A`
    `a refusal to approve a branch under section 9`
    `a refusal to approve a change of name or rules under section 11`
    `a refusal to consent to the use of a flag, symbol or insignia under section 13`
    `an order to furnish information under section 10`
    `an order to change name or rules under section 11A`
    `a declaration that a person is unfit to be an officer under section 12(1)(b)`
    `an order of dissolution under section 24`

GIVEN `the decision` IS A Decision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act provides an appeal to the Minister` IF
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `a refusal to register a specified society under section 4` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a refusal to register a society under section 4A` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a refusal to approve a branch under section 9` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a refusal to approve a change of name or rules under section 11` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a refusal to consent to the use of a flag, symbol or insignia under section 13` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the decision` IS A Decision
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the number of days allowed for the appeal` IS
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `a refusal to register a specified society under section 4` THEN JUST 30
    WHEN `a refusal to register a society under section 4A` THEN JUST 30
    WHEN `a refusal to approve a branch under section 9` THEN JUST 30
    WHEN `a refusal to approve a change of name or rules under section 11` THEN JUST 30
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

GIVEN `the decision` IS A Decision, `days since the decision` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an appeal is in time` IF
    IF   NOT `the Act provides an appeal to the Minister` `the decision`
    THEN FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER `the number of days allowed for the appeal` `the decision`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
         WHEN JUST `n` THEN `days since the decision` AT MOST `n`

§§ `6, 7 -- ceasing to exist, and dissolving`

-- s 6(1): where the Registrar or an Assistant Registrar "has reason to believe that any registered
-- society has ceased to exist, he may publish in the Gazette a notification calling upon the
-- society to furnish him with proof of its existence within 3 months"; (1A) a copy must be sent to
-- the registered address or by email.
-- s 6(2): "If at the expiration of the 3 months the Registrar is satisfied that the society has
-- ceased to exist, a notification to that effect shall be published in the Gazette, and the society
-- shall be DEEMED TO HAVE CEASED TO EXIST FROM THE DATE OF THE PUBLICATION."
--
-- The deeming runs from the second publication and does not depend on the society having actually
-- ceased. A society that never saw the notices, or answered inadequately, and is in fact active,
-- is deemed to have ceased and is no longer a registered society. That makes it an unlawful society
-- under s 14(1), and its members and managers offenders.
DECLARE CessationFacts HAS
    `the Registrar published a notification calling for proof of existence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a copy was sent to the registered address or by email` IS A BOOLEAN
    `months since the notification` IS A NUMBER
    `the society furnished proof of its existence within 3 months` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Registrar is satisfied the society has ceased to exist` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a second notification was published in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the society is in fact still active` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS A CessationFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the society is deemed to have ceased to exist` IF
        `the facts`'s `the Registrar published a notification calling for proof of existence`
    AND `the facts`'s `months since the notification` AT LEAST 3
    AND `the facts`'s `the Registrar is satisfied the society has ceased to exist`
    AND `the facts`'s `a second notification was published in the Gazette`

-- The Act does not make the deeming depend on the society's actual condition, and does not make a
-- failure to send the copy under s 6(1A) a bar to the deeming.
GIVEN `the facts` IS A CessationFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the deeming depends on the society having actually ceased` IF
    FALSE

GIVEN `the facts` IS A CessationFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a failure to send the copy under section 6(1A) prevents the deeming` IF
    FALSE

-- s 7(1): a registered society that proposes to dissolve itself voluntarily in accordance with its
-- rules "shall inform the Registrar in writing, and a certificate of dissolution, SIGNED BY THE
-- PRESIDENT, THE SECRETARY AND THE TREASURER or officers holding analogous positions, shall be sent
-- to the Registrar WITHIN ONE WEEK of the society's dissolution."
-- s 7(2): on receiving it, the Registrar shall, "if he is satisfied that the society has been
-- dissolved in accordance with its rules", publish a notification declaring that it has ceased.
DECLARE VoluntaryDissolution HAS
    `the Registrar was informed in writing of the proposal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the president signed the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the secretary signed the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the treasurer signed the certificate` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days between the dissolution and sending the certificate` IS A NUMBER
    `the Registrar is satisfied it was dissolved in accordance with its rules` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the dissolution` IS A VoluntaryDissolution
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the certificate meets section 7(1)` IF
        `the dissolution`'s `the president signed the certificate`
    AND `the dissolution`'s `the secretary signed the certificate`
    AND `the dissolution`'s `the treasurer signed the certificate`
    AND `the dissolution`'s `days between the dissolution and sending the certificate` AT MOST 7

GIVEN `the dissolution` IS A VoluntaryDissolution
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar must publish the notification under section 7(2)` IF
        `the certificate meets section 7(1)` `the dissolution`
    AND `the dissolution`'s `the Registrar is satisfied it was dissolved in accordance with its rules`

§§ `8 -- inspecting a society's documents`

-- s 8(1): "any person may on payment of the prescribed fees inspect any document in the possession of
-- the Registrar ... received from any registered society and be supplied with a copy".
-- s 8(3): "No person shall be allowed to inspect the ACCOUNTS of a registered society ... unless the
-- Registrar is satisfied that the person is a MEMBER of the society."
GIVEN `the document is the society's accounts` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the person is a member of the society` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may inspect the document` IF
    IF   `the document is the society's accounts`
    THEN `the person is a member of the society`
    ELSE TRUE

§§ `9 -- branches`

-- s 9(1): "No registered society shall establish a branch without the prior approval of the Registrar."
-- s 9(2): the Registrar may refuse if (a) the rules do not provide for a branch, or (b) the branch's
-- rules would make it an independent society not adequately under the society's control.
-- s 9(3): "Where a registered society establishes a branch without the prior approval of the Registrar,
-- the branch so established shall be DEEMED TO BE AN UNLAWFUL SOCIETY."
--
-- The consequence of an unapproved branch is not a fine on the parent but the branch's outlawing,
-- with every consequence of s 14 for those who join or run it.
GIVEN `the Registrar gave prior approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the branch is deemed an unlawful society under section 9(3)` IF
    NOT `the Registrar gave prior approval`

GIVEN `the rules provide for a branch` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the branch's rules would make it an independent society not adequately under the society's control` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Registrar may refuse to approve the branch` IF
        NOT `the rules provide for a branch`
    OR  `the branch's rules would make it an independent society not adequately under the society's control`

§§ `10 -- information the Registrar can demand`

-- s 10(1): the Registrar or an Assistant Registrar "may at any time by written notice order any
-- registered society to furnish him with any such information as he may require concerning the
-- society (such as but not limited to the patron ... and every person managing or assisting in the
-- management ...) or any documents, accounts and books".
-- s 10(2): the obligation "shall be binding upon EVERY OFFICER, and upon every person managing or
-- assisting in the management, of that society in Singapore."
-- s 10(3): if the society fails to comply, "EACH of the persons mentioned in subsection (2) WHO HAS
-- BEEN SERVED WITH THE ORDER" is guilty of an offence: a fine not exceeding $10,000 "unless he
-- ESTABLISHES TO THE SATISFACTION OF THE COURT that he has exercised due diligence and has failed to
-- comply with the order for reasons beyond his control."
-- s 10(4): a person who in response to the order (a) intentionally alters, suppresses or destroys
-- information or a document, account or book required, or (b) makes a statement the person knows or
-- ought reasonably to know is, or is reckless as to whether it is, false or misleading in a
-- material particular, commits an offence: a fine not exceeding $10,000 or imprisonment not
-- exceeding 12 months or both.
--
-- Liability under s 10(3) is personal, individual, and falls on everyone served -- not only on the
-- officer who had the documents. The burden of the due-diligence defence is on the person.
DECLARE OrderFacts HAS
    `the society failed to comply with the whole or part of the order` IS A BOOLEAN
    `this person is an officer or a person managing or assisting in the management in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `this person was served with the order` IS A BOOLEAN
    `this person establishes due diligence and that non-compliance was for reasons beyond their control` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS AN OrderFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person commits the offence in section 10(3)` IF
        `the facts`'s `the society failed to comply with the whole or part of the order`
    AND `the facts`'s `this person is an officer or a person managing or assisting in the management in Singapore`
    AND `the facts`'s `this person was served with the order`
    AND NOT `the facts`'s `this person establishes due diligence and that non-compliance was for reasons beyond their control`

DECLARE FalseResponseFacts HAS
    `intentionally altered, suppressed or destroyed something required by the order` IS A BOOLEAN
    `made a statement in response that is false or misleading in a material particular` IS A BOOLEAN
    `knew, ought reasonably to have known, or was reckless as to whether it was false or misleading` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS A FalseResponseFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person commits the offence in section 10(4)` IF
        `the facts`'s `intentionally altered, suppressed or destroyed something required by the order`
    OR  (    `the facts`'s `made a statement in response that is false or misleading in a material particular`
         AND `the facts`'s `knew, ought reasonably to have known, or was reckless as to whether it was false or misleading`)

§§ `11, 11A -- changing a name or rules`

-- s 11(1): "No registered society shall -- (a) change its name; or (b) amend its rules, without the
-- PRIOR APPROVAL IN WRITING of the Registrar or an Assistant Registrar."
-- s 11(2): if it fails, "the society and EVERY OFFICER of the society shall be guilty of an offence and
-- shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $6,000." There is no due-diligence defence.
-- s 11(3): "amend" includes making a new rule and rescinding an existing rule.
-- s 11A: for a society registered under s 4A, the Registrar may at any time by written notice ORDER it
-- to change its name (if misleading, undesirable or offensive, identical, or suggesting a Government
-- connection that does not exist) or amend its rules (if contrary to national security or interest,
-- prejudicial to public peace, welfare or good order, or contrary to the Act). 11A(4): failure is an
-- offence by the society and every officer, fine not exceeding $6,000; 11A(5): "it shall be a defence
-- for [an officer] to establish ... that he has exercised due diligence and has failed to comply ... for
-- reasons beyond his control."
--
-- The two offences are the same size ($6,000) and the same shape (society and every officer). The
-- difference is that an officer charged under s 11A has a due-diligence defence and an officer
-- charged under s 11(2) has none, although s 11(2)'s officer may have had no say in the society's
-- decision to change a rule.
DECLARE ChangeFacts HAS
    `the society changed its name or amended its rules` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Registrar or an Assistant Registrar gave prior approval in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
    `this person is an officer of the society` IS A BOOLEAN
    `this person had no part in the decision` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS A ChangeFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the society and this officer commit the offence in section 11(2)` IF
        `the facts`'s `the society changed its name or amended its rules`
    AND NOT `the facts`'s `the Registrar or an Assistant Registrar gave prior approval in writing`
    AND `the facts`'s `this person is an officer of the society`

GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an officer charged under section 11(2) has a due-diligence defence` IF
    FALSE

DECLARE NoticeFacts HAS
    `the society is registered under section 4A` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a written notice was given under section 11A` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the society failed to comply with it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `this person is an officer of the society` IS A BOOLEAN
    `this person establishes due diligence and that non-compliance was for reasons beyond their control` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the facts` IS A NoticeFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the society commits the offence in section 11A(4)` IF
        `the facts`'s `the society is registered under section 4A`
    AND `the facts`'s `a written notice was given under section 11A`
    AND `the facts`'s `the society failed to comply with it`

GIVEN `the facts` IS A NoticeFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this officer commits the offence in section 11A(4)` IF
        `the society commits the offence in section 11A(4)` `the facts`
    AND `the facts`'s `this person is an officer of the society`
    AND NOT `the facts`'s `this person establishes due diligence and that non-compliance was for reasons beyond their control`

§§ `12 -- persons who may not act as officers`

-- s 12(1): "no person shall act as an officer of a registered society or a branch thereof if -- (a) he
-- has, while being a member of a society, been convicted for an offence involving the UNLAWFUL
-- EXPENDITURE OF THE FUNDS of the society; or (b) he has been DECLARED, IN WRITING, BY THE REGISTRAR to
-- be unfit to act as an officer of a society by reason of any conviction for a criminal offence other
-- than that specified in paragraph (a)."
-- s 12(1A) and (1B): a prohibited person may apply to the Minister for permission, which "may be granted
-- ... if the Minister thinks fit".
-- s 12(2): acting in contravention is an offence: a fine not exceeding $10,000 or imprisonment not
-- exceeding 2 years or both.
--
-- Limb (a) operates by itself on the conviction. Limb (b) needs a written declaration by the Registrar,
-- and so the same bad conduct outside the funds offence disqualifies only once declared.
DECLARE OfficerFacts HAS
    `convicted, while a member of a society, of an offence involving unlawful expenditure of its funds` IS A BOOLEAN
    `convicted of some other criminal offence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `declared in writing by the Registrar to be unfit by reason of that other conviction` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the Minister has granted permission` IS A BOOLEAN
    `acting as an officer of a registered society or a branch` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the person` IS AN OfficerFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is prohibited from acting as an officer` IF
        `the person`'s `convicted, while a member of a society, of an offence involving unlawful expenditure of its funds`
    OR  (    `the person`'s `convicted of some other criminal offence`
         AND `the person`'s `declared in writing by the Registrar to be unfit by reason of that other conviction`)

GIVEN `the person` IS AN OfficerFacts
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person commits the offence in section 12(2)` IF
        `the person`'s `acting as an officer of a registered society or a branch`
    AND `the person is prohibited from acting as an officer` `the person`
    AND NOT `the person`'s `the Minister has granted permission`

§§ `13 -- flags, symbols and insignia`

-- s 13(1): "No registered society shall use any flag, symbol, emblem, badge or other insignia without the
-- consent in writing of the Registrar or an Assistant Registrar."
-- s 13(3): where a registered society uses one in contravention -- "(a) the officers of the society; and
-- (b) all persons managing or assisting in the management of the society, shall be DEEMED to be guilty
-- of an offence": a fine not exceeding $6,000 or imprisonment not exceeding one year or both.
-- s 13(2): an appeal lies to the Minister, no period stated.
--
-- The liability is deemed and attaches to the officers and the managers, not to the person who made or
-- displayed the item.
GIVEN `the society used a flag, symbol, emblem, badge or other insignia` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the Registrar or an Assistant Registrar consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `this person is an officer or a person managing or assisting in the management` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `this person is deemed guilty under section 13(3)` IF
        `the society used a flag, symbol, emblem, badge or other insignia`
    AND NOT `the Registrar or an Assistant Registrar consented in writing`
    AND `this person is an officer or a person managing or assisting in the management`
